# The row lake is committed on purpose: Vercel cannot write at runtime, so the
# deployed site is built from these snapshots, and a scheduled job refreshes
# them by committing. It is small (under a megabyte for a full season).
# Blobs are the exception: 119MB of player photos do not belong in git, and
# the site loads them from the Premier League CDN instead.
